<title>USA: Thermedics gets bomb detection contract.</title>
<headline>Thermedics gets bomb detection contract.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermedics Detection Inc, a subsidiary of Thermedics Inc, said on Tuesday it has a contract to develop a portable EGIS bomb-detection system for the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration.</p>
<p>Thermedics said the contract is worth more than $700,00 and calls for a portable system to screen explosives at airports, border crossings and other checkpoints.</p>
<p>Thermedics said its EGIS system is now used to scan carry-on and checked baggage. There are more than 185 EGIS systems now in use, the company said.</p>
</text>
